# .understandignore — patterns for files/dirs to exclude from analysis
# Syntax: same as .gitignore (globs, # comments, ! negation, trailing / for dirs)
#
# Built-in defaults already exclude: node_modules/, .git/, dist/, build/, obj/,
# *.lock, *.min.js, images, fonts, etc. — but Android adds a lot more cache state
# that the defaults don't know about. Tuned for this monorepo below.

# --- Android / Gradle build state (filesystem walk picks these up) ---
.gradle/
.kotlin/
**/.gradle/
**/.kotlin/
**/build/
android/app/build/
android/build/
android/build-logic/.gradle/
captures/
release/
*.apk
*.aab
*.ap_
*.dex
.cxx/

# --- IDE noise (gitignored but may be present locally) ---
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iws
*.iml
*.ipr

# --- Raw 2048² Gemini PNGs — too big and not part of the shipping app ---
temp-asset/*.png
temp-asset/*.jpg
temp-asset/*.jpeg

# --- macOS turds ---
.DS_Store

# --- (Intentionally keep) ---
# docs/                  — ARCHITECTURE / PROGRESS are essential context
# spec/                  — pairing protocol + MCP tools are part of the design
# temp-asset/process.py  — the illustration pipeline IS shippable knowledge
# **/src/test/           — keep test files; they document expected behaviour
# **/src/androidTest/    — same
# Anything in android/{app,core,feature,data-source,build-logic}/src/
# Anything in relay-server/{cmd,internal,deploy}/
